    "details": {
      "alignment": "Lawful Evil",
      "type": {
        "value": "humanoid",
        "subtype": "Beanish"
      },
      "cr": 5,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Fawful's Forces packet sheet — Maestro Mustardo.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-forge-packets.py</code> from the NPC Forge roster <code>data/forge/fawfuls-forces.json</code> (entry <code>maestro-mustardo</code>): Small humanoid (Beanish), Lawful Evil; CR 5 (proficiency +3, to hit +4 with DEX); AC 15 (apron of armour plates (breastplate)), hit points 82 (15d6+30), speed 30 ft.. A GM scene kit for the Fawful's Forces article's present (1040 BF), not a filed event; the faction article stays the authority.</p><p>Master of the castle's cannon crews and, by his own appointment, of its kitchens. Mustardo was a Beanish artillery sergeant who understood two things about his lord — that Fawful hates mustard, and that Fawful loves fury — and built a career on serving both: the Mustard Sprayers are his recipe, the Boom-Crawlers are his drill, and the main cannon fires when his whistle says so. He conducts a battle like an overture, baton lit.</p><p>As a fight he is a support piece who hurts. The cannon call is announced a round early — the party sees the marker, and the question is whether they can move everyone and still finish him. Bloodying him makes everything around him worse (Fury Rising), so either burst him down from full or pull him away from his machines first. He surrenders only in the sense that he keeps talking.</p><p><strong>Role:</strong> artillery officer · <strong>tier:</strong> lieutenant · <strong>folder:</strong> Fawful's Furious Freaks / Lieutenants of Fury.</p><h3>Art</h3><p>Token plate <code>portraits/fawfuls-forces/maestro-mustardo.png</code> — NPC Forge render, seed 410011, cut from a flat #FF00FF field. Prompt: <q>Clean cel-shaded cartoon character art in the style of Mario & Luigi RPG concept art, bold dark outlines, flat colours, simple shading. A small lime-green bean-shaped Beanish officer with a monocle and a mad grin, wearing a mustard-yellow long military coat with brass epaulettes over an apron made of armour plates, a tall chef-general's hat with a brass cannon badge, holding up a conductor's baton that is a lit sparking fuse, with a backpack of mustard tanks and hoses, conducting pose. Full body, whole figure visible, three-quarter view, centred, isolated on a plain flat solid magenta background (#FF00FF), no floor, no ground shadow, no text, no border.</q></p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
